Print an oc access descriptor for independent operator execution; do not launch a client or connect. Success prints a bounded access descriptor for independent operator execution. Use -- before a flag-shaped first payload value to preserve it as data. After the first payload value, all remaining tokens belong to the payload. Applicable to OpenShift/OKD ContainerClusters only.. This command is recognized but not implemented.

Usage:
  bootwright cluster oc <command>... [flags]

Flags:
      --name string   Select the exact object name (required)

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
